i suppose rumors have been going around  haven't they for a couple of weeks about  this development but confirmation coming  just a couple of hours ago  yeah they certainly have and it is no  real surprise that there won't be any  overseas spectators  at either the olympics or the  paralympics this summer it's a decision  that's been foreshadowed by the japanese  media  for several weeks now and my  understanding is that the tokyo  organizing committee  felt like they had to come to this  decision to give the best possible  chance  for the olympics and paralympics to go  ahead this summer in any iteration at  all  nevertheless it will be upsetting to  those die hard fans who go to the  olympic host city  every four years and buy tickets to see  events there it's also upsetting for the  families of some of the competitors  some of these athletes will only go to  an olympics once in their career  and this would would have been a chance  for their loved ones  to see them at the very pinnacle of  their career on the biggest stage  at all but as i said no real surprise  um obviously with questions about  whether this olympics will go ahead  still raging now the tokyo organizing  committee have released a statement  explaining their decision they said the  kovid 19 situation  around the world is still very  challenging and a number of variant  strains have emerged  while international travel remains  severely restricted globally  based on the present situation it's  highly unlikely that entry into japan  will be guaranteed this summer  for people from overseas in order to  give clarity to ticket holders  parties on the japanese side have come  to the conclusion that they will not be  able to enter japan at the time of the  olympic and paralympic  games my understanding is that they'd  already sold approximately 1 million  tickets to  international spectators 4.5 million  tickets  have been sold to japanese spectators  with decisions still to be taken  or whether domestic fans will be able to  be inside those arenas  for the olympics and paralympics and  there's still  huge resistance in japan this olympics  taking place at all  and they've been several polls done now  which indicate an  overwhelming majority of people don't  want this olympics to happen in japan  and that's easy to understand because  japan has  kept this pandemic relatively under  control  they still have a horrific death toll um  around 8  700 deaths as a result of coving 19 but  that's nothing compared to the toll  we've seen it take  in europe usa central and south america  so you can understand why many japanese  people  don't want 15 000 athletes arriving in  tokyo  the world's most crowded metropolitan  area this summer  that's without considering the tens of  thousands of officials  journalists and media as well that would  be  arriving into japan um so the tokyo  olympic committee the japanese  government and also the international  olympic committee  still determined that this olympics will  go ahead in some shape or form
 

